WEBVTT

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:05.090
This is my other self from the Frontier world...

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.000
Doctor Odhner.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:13.840
That's right. We decided to join forces
to stop you guys from running rampant.

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.010
You're an intelligent boy.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:21.390
You're aware of which choice
is the most beneficial, yes?

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.560
<i>Don't do it, Kazasumi!</i>

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.310
Kumi!

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.520
<i>Please escape!</i>

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.280
He's never been satisfied
with Kyohma being in charge.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.740
Let's stop the doctor.
First, we have to get everyone together.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.120
Now, I leave everything up to you, Tohru...

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:39.080
Kyoka!

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.590
All we need to do is wait...

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:52.550
...for all of you to reach the Dead End.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.440
Counterattack: The Destination of Emotions

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.490
The coast looks clear.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.620
Yeah...

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:51.840
Are you all right?

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.050
Yeah. I think I overexerted myself a bit.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.930
Hi you two!

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.020
You were waiting for us?

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.400
That's...

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:13.860
Lyudmila's?

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.610
What... happened?

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.200
I've already avenged her.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.460
What is this place?

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:39.670
A hitman for hire is often
betrayed by their sponsors.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:45.560
A professional always has one
or two safehouses ready to use.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.560
Thank you for saving us.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.070
Guiding the students is part
of a teacher's job.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.570
Though, it might become
"former" teacher before too long.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.110
Are you planning
to start a war or something?

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:05.780
Don't forget...
they're the ones that instigated this.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.370
Anyway, is the princess all right?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.540
Kyoka!

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:13.710
I'm fine.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.460
You're not fine! Your face is so pale!

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.130
She looks tired.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.260
There's a bedroom past that staircase.
Make sure she rests.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.090
Got it.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.510
Let's go. Can you stand?

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.890
Don't you two engage in
any "tiring activities," okay?

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.020
We won't!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.200
<i>Really... You're always surprising me.</i>

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:59.840
Chief... Chief... Chief!

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.130
Chief! I've been looking for you!

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.560
The results of the biomolecular motor
adsorption experiments are in.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.600
I guess it's time for that already.
What's the fluctuation on the Galvanic waves?

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:19.320
From #1 to #50,
the margin of error is within 0.001 percent.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.240
In the Simulacra tests, there was zero percent error.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:24.820
So is that the prodigy
from the nano-biomechanical engineering lab?

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.410
Is that so?
This is the first I've seen her.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.410
I want a thorough investigation
of the data immediately.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.250
She's usually cooped up in a lab
and hardly ever comes out.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.120
<i>The discovery of the Energy Cube,</i>

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:39.000
<i>and the miraculous advances
in scientific technology that followed...</i>

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:44.470
<i>...gave us the means
to traverse time and space.</i>

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.310
<i>The discovery of another world,
exactly like our own...</i>

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:54.430
<i>However, that was
a very unfortunate encounter.</i>

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.770
<i>In the long, harsh war,
I lost my parents as well.</i>

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:07.990
<i>In the midst of that, I was researching a technology
in order to save the people.</i>

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:15.250
<i>A bio-nanomachine that can analyze genetic data
and recreate lost body parts...</i>

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:20.290
<i>With our technology advanced by the Energy Cubes,</i>

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.670
<i>I was able to complete that research.</i>

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.840
Are these that girl's memories?

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.430
What is this?

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:38.140
What's the meaning of this?
I wasn't told anything!

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:45.110
<i>Medical technology is easily adapted
for military purposes.</i>

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.200
<i>That was the Dead End...</i>

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:57.830
<i>The beginning of the death
that guides everything to its end.</i>

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:03.380
<i>It didn't take long until the humans
who turned into nano-machines</i>

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.460
<i>engulfed the entire world.</i>

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:10.180
All of these people too...

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:13.430
Hurry! They're coming!

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:14.890
Understood!

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.230
I'm sorry to make you do this for me...

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:27.070
Doctor, you are humanity's last hope.
We must find a means to combat them at any cost...

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:34.780
<i>I devoted myself to a resistance organization.</i>

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:02.600
<i>I'll stop them, no matter what!</i>

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:18.330
<i>It all started with our mistake.</i>

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.210
<i>But...</i>

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:31.720
See that girl over there?
Someone like her...

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.300
HELP

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.930
<i>Help me.</i>

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:40.770
It's you!

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:41.600
<i>The future...</i>

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.440
Your voice, to me,
is the same as the Timekeepers.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:48.070
It's meaningless noise
with nothing to back it up.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.860
<i>My voice isn't reaching anyone.</i>

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:57.330
<i>Someone, help... me, and the future...</i>

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:58.830
<i>It's all right!</i>

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.130
Tohru has the power to change the future.
So, you should believe in him, too!

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.670
Let's stop the Timekeepers.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.630
Please go to that place.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:14.720
That place?

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.950
Morning, Kyoka.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.120
Morning, Tohru.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.750
So Aaron and the others are safe as well?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:53.260
Yes. I heard from Kumi's group as well.
Apparently your brother is with them, too.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.380
He really is impossible to kill.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:58.760
Where is the rendezvous point?

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.850
Let's see... it should be
coming up about now.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.560
Just now... that was Kumi's doing?

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:15.610
Yes. She was basically responsible
for setting up all of the security for that lab,

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:18.700
so this is like her backyard as well.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:26.960
This is a shelter that was
abandoned during the civil war.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:31.290
Melchizedek requisitioned it and
equipped it with a maintenance module.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.430
Tohru, and Kyoka too!

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:38.220
Kyoka!

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.930
I'm glad! You really are alive!

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:45.730
Yeah... it's good to see you again, Remy.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:50.650
Geez, I told you that you can't eat
or drink in this room.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.110
Sorry, but I got hungry.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:58.490
We were devoting all our time to removing
the control mechanisms that were on the guns.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.620
But doesn't it smell delicious?

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.200
It's frozen food that was stockpiled here.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.910
There's still plenty left
in that freezer over there.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.460
I'm glad that you guys
managed to stay safe.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:13.040
But... Lyudmila...

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.640
My sister!

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:33.020
As I just explained, our current situation is such
that if the Timekeepers aren't stopped,

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:36.320
world history will no doubt
be shaped exactly to their liking.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.900
So combat is inevitable.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.610
For now, there are two things we can do.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.830
One, defeat the Timekeepers
and remove all of their interference.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:50.960
At the same time, we need to get rid of Dr. Odhner
and destroy the time machine.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:55.800
If we're going to destroy the time machine,
how are we going to go to the past?

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.340
I've got a good lead for that.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.300
Do we have a specific method
to defeat the Timekeepers?

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.180
We do.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:08.310
I'll explain that right now.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:17.360
We're ready over here.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.900
Please hold on for just a moment.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:23.160
I'm going to run a few
more dummy processes first.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:27.240
Is it really all right for
just the two of you to go?

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:32.420
I left a lot of presents behind at the lab,
so I'm sure we can get in somehow.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:36.380
To be honest, I'm overwhelmed by the
desire to run away from all this,

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:38.880
but there are things that only I can do.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.630
Can I ask one thing?

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.590
I can understand the reason
for Kumi to defect to our side.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.300
What's the reasoning behind your switch?

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.270
Let's see...

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:53.230
How about because they're 
disrespecting my little sister's death?

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:58.230
I find it hard to believe you've got that
kind of heart, you homicidal maniac.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.860
How rude...

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:04.240
Well, let's leave it at that for now.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.240
Tohru!

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:12.290
Hey, you haven't eaten yet, right?

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.460
Kyoka...

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.750
I found a good spot.
Why don't we check it out?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.710
There's still time left
before the operation starts.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:20.960
It's fine; go ahead.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.840
Come on! This way, this way!

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.090
Hold on!

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:26.550
Hurry, hurry!

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:32.560
She's gonna have him on
a leash before too long.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:38.020
Ta-da! Isn't this amazing?

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:43.650
Kumi told me about this place.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:46.240
She said this was an evacuation shelter.

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:50.700
Maybe even after escaping into a place like this,
they wanted to live the same as they did aboveground.

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:55.460
They don't look like fake flowers.
They seem so real.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.130
Oh, a bee...

00:13:58.460 --> 00:13:59.420
Just kidding.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.300
Geez!

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.930
It feels like so much time
has passed since back then.

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:08.970
It hasn't even been a month, right?

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:14.230
We used to talk at school,
or make little stops on the way home,

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:19.020
but we never went out
to have fun by ourselves like this.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.150
You're right.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:24.400
But it's always fun to be with you. Even now...

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:29.200
Tohru, you suddenly got good
at dealing with girls.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.790
Fess up! Where did you acquire those skills?

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:33.950
Where, you ask?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:41.040
Okay, that expression gives you away!
Whose face did you think of just now?

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:44.340
Well, um, it was technically your face.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:46.880
That's the look you have when you lie!

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.590
Tell me!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:48.590
Hold—

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.830
This is kind of weird, isn't it?

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:16.910
What is?

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:22.460
The last battle to decide the fate of the world is coming up soon, right? But...

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:24.590
We're on a date, and arguing with each other...

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:28.220
This is amazing.
I'm on a date with Tohru right now.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.930
Is where you were shot okay?

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.390
Yeah, I'm fine now.

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:39.890
I'm apparently going to end up
with a small scar, though.

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:41.310
I'm sorry.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.440
I'll protect you this time.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:45.320
Thank you.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.900
In return, I'll protect you too, Tohru.

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:52.910
Hey, you're still worried
about something, aren't you?

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.330
You can tell?

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:55.990
I can tell.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:58.250
You have that look on your face
when you're worried about things.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:01.830
I just can't stop myself from thinking about it.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:07.960
Just as Kyohma and the others said:
we fight, and we win, but that's not the end.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:15.970
If what happened to Remy is what's going to happen to the world... what can I do?

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:20.730
Tohru, you went to the other world
and saw it for yourself, right?

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:23.520
Was it completely different from here?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:28.940
Yeah. Everything was in ruins,
and it was a very difficult place to survive...

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:31.990
But some things were the same.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:35.910
And everyone there was trying as hard as they could to survive.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:37.490
I see...

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:46.710
Personally, I don't think we need to change the entire future ourselves.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.590
If we can just make it so things go just a little bit differently...

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:53.970
I'm sure that the people of the future
will do their best, too.

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:55.970
You think so?

00:16:56.680 --> 00:17:00.230
Besides, I've met my other self as well.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:07.110
Our other selves are the result of history turning out a different way,

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:10.900
which means mankind has infinite possibilities!

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:12.650
You're right...

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.030
You really are right.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:20.080
Besides, I told you before, right?

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:26.670
"You should just become the president or something,
Tohru, and change the world!"

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.670
I love you.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:33.760
I love you too.

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:37.800
Please keep caring for me.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:39.760
Please do so too.

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:47.560
What happened to the partition?
Can't you just cut off this sector?

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.860
No good. The security has been compromised!

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:56.450
Have those that went after Katagiri's group
return to the lab!

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:02.870
And now it's certain.
They are enemies of the whole world.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:08.000
We must get rid of every time-transfer eligible person
and eradicate them from history, or our future...

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.050
Maybe so.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:14.880
You!

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:18.430
It's not that I dislike men
whose egos have grown to be enormous...

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:19.350
...but, I'm sorry.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:22.270
It's an intruder! Restrain her!

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:25.480
What are you doing!
Olga Janetine is right he—

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:41.660
I suppose it's not like me
to do something like this, Sidune...

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:54.760
We're much obliged to you, Brian Odhner.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.590
But I'll choose the future that I believe in.

00:18:58.590 --> 00:19:00.100
Was this the right thing to do?

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:03.810
You're going to walk
down this path with me, right?

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:10.270
Tohru, your future is my future.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:16.780
HELP

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:14.820
What can you tell?

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:19.780
I feel an immense power,
just like what was inside the time machine.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:26.580
This is... an expanded version of the Penrose equation?
This is the basic theory behind time travel!

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:42.180
Are we good to go?

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:46.060
It's fine. I'm sure that it's the 21st century
on the other side.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.890
Come to think of it, there's something
I've been forgetting to ask.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.190
What is it?

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.440
How are we getting back?

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.280
We're not coming back.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:58.490
Just kidding.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:01.200
If we can get that huge Energy Cube,

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:05.040
I'm sure we can somehow make a time machine
even if this hole collapses.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:06.410
Or so we hope...

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.160
Basically, we just have to win.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:09.710
Yeah.

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:12.540
Okay, we'll go first!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:14.540
Don't be late!

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:18.340
Oh, brother. Guess I'll go, too.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.550
See you later, comrades.

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:21.760
Me, too!

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.850
Hold it! Don't leave me behind!

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:25.180
All right, I'm going, too.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.140
Grit your teeth!

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.100
We'll call it even for now.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:34.020
But it's not like
I approve of you just yet.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:35.860
You saw us?

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:40.280
Prove to me that
you're a man worthy of Kyoka.

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.120
You don't have to tell me that.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:08.140
<i>If another me was born somewhere else,
and had led a different life, how would he feel?</i>

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:12.980
<i>If there was another version of myself
somewhere on the other side of the ocean,</i>

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:15.440
<i>what would happen
if I were able to meet him?</i>

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:18.820
<i>Would I be able to be his friend?</i>

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:23.360
<i>Or would the differences in our upbringing
be something that I couldn't overcome?</i>

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.620
<i>Can I understand him because he is me?</i>

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.960
<i>Or will he be impossible to
understand because he's me?</i>

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.710
<i>Even then, I...</i>

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:45.930
I'll do as much as I can do!

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:28.740
Since the story is nearing its climax, we should fight
as well to settle the score once and for all!

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:31.830
The feeling that this day would come at some point...
was not really in my mind.

00:23:31.830 --> 00:23:34.870
The mascot that wins
will acquire his ideal future!

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:37.210
It's too troublesome.
I'm okay with how it is now.

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:38.250
Next episode: "Showdown."

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:39.920
<b><i>SHOWDOWN </i></b>AT THE END OF TIME

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:39.920
"At the End of Time."
